<h1>🐦 Twitties</h1>

<p class="text-muted">
  A small social app running on a load-balanced, auto-scaled AWS deployment.
</p>

<p>Click <a href="/posts">here</a> to view the latest twitties.</p>

<hr class="my-4">

<h5 class="mb-3">Live system status</h5>

<ul class="list-unstyled">
  <li class="mb-1"><b>Backend: <%= backend ? "✅" : "💥" %></b></li>
  <li class="mb-1"><b>Backend &rarr; Database: <%= db ? "✅" : "💥" %></b></li>
</ul>

<div class="card border-0" style="background-color: #f7f9f9;">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h6 class="card-title mb-2">Served by</h6>
    <ul class="list-unstyled mb-2 font-monospace small">
      <li>frontend instance: <%= frontendHost %></li>
      <li>backend instance:&nbsp; <%= backendHost %></li>
    </ul>
    <small class="text-muted">
      Each tier runs behind its own load balancer across multiple instances.
      Refresh this page and these identifiers will change as requests are
      distributed to different servers.
    </small>
  </div>
</div>
